  "turn_number": 3,
  "player_text": "The track itself tells me nothing, so I walk into the crate yards and look between the stacks, checking the gaps and the ground behind them for anything the rain and wagon ruts would not have wiped away.",
  "visible_motivation": "The warning named the crate yards, and the open mud only shows ordinary wagon and laborer traffic.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want to see whether something is hidden, dropped, or out of place among the crates themselves.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "You weave carefully through the narrow aisles between towering stacks of crates in the muddy yard. The rain has blurred most prints and wiped away any fresh clues from the ground. Despite the recent wagon traffic, no obvious signs betray hurried passage or struggle among the piles. Between the staggered crates, scattered broken packing straw curls damply, yet you find no unusual footprints or traces left by the missing patrol. The air here carries the sharp scent of wood and rope, mingled with the pervasive cold dampness—a stagnant silence lingering beneath the watchful eyes of nearby guards.",
